#, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/devices/cluster.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several charge points"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Surplus charging and phase switching (EVSE)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"With surplus charging, the electric car charges as far as possible with "
"**solar power that would otherwise be fed into the grid**. To make this work "
"even with little sun, the wallbox can **switch between single-phase and "
"three-phase charging**. This page explains how OpenEMS proceeds. It "
"describes the new charge point control “EVSE” (functions "
"**Evse.Controller.Single** per charge point and **Evse.Controller.Cluster** "
"for all charge points together)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The charging modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mode\n"
"| Behavior\n"
"\n"
"| **PV Surplus** (“Surplus” in the configuration)\n"
"| Only charges with surplus. If it is not sufficient for the minimum power of the car, charging pauses.\n"
"| **PV Surplus with guaranteed charge** (“Minimum” in the configuration)\n"
"| Always charges at least at the lowest possible power, from the grid or storage if necessary. Additional surplus is used on top.\n"
"| **Fast Charging** (“Force” in the configuration)\n"
"| Charges immediately at full power, regardless of the surplus.\n"
"| **No Charge** (“Zero” in the configuration)\n"
"| Does not charge.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"The mode can be permanently set, changed via a time schedule (“Schedule” in "
"the web interface) or specified once for the current charging session (“One-"
"Shot”, applies until the cable is unplugged). Optionally, an energy limit "
"can be set per charging session, e.g. “at most 20 kWh”."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What counts as surplus"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-counts-as-surplus
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "OpenEMS calculates the available surplus every second as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Surplus = current charging power of the cars\n"
"        + feed-in to the grid\n"
"        + charging power of the home storage\n"
"        − purchase from the grid\n"
"        − discharge power of the home storage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "It follows that:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**The car has priority over the home storage.** Power currently flowing into "
"the home storage counts as surplus and can go to the car."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**The home storage is not discharged into the car during surplus charging.** "
"If the storage discharges, this reduces the surplus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"Purchase from the grid reduces the surplus. If grid purchase is greater than "
"the current charging power, no surplus remains."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sequence of surplus charging"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting charging"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-starting-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "A paused charging session only starts when"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-starting-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"there was enough surplus for the minimum power for at least 90 % of the time "
"in the last 20 seconds"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-starting-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "and continuously in the last 10 seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pausing charging"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pausing-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "A running charging session is only paused when"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pausing-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"there was insufficient surplus for at least 90 % of the time in the last "
"minute"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pausing-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "and continuously none in the last 10 seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-pausing-charging
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "Until then, the car continues charging at minimum power."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lock time after start or pause"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-lock-time-after-start-or-pause
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"After each start or pause triggered by the surplus, a **lock time of 5 "
"minutes** applies. No further change takes place during this time. This "
"protects the car and wallbox when clouds pass by."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-lock-time-after-start-or-pause
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Consequence:** Shortly after a start, the car can continue charging at "
"minimum power for up to 5 minutes even though the surplus has already gone. "
"This energy then comes from the grid or the home storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adjusting the power"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adjusting-the-power
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"More power is released **gently**, at most about 3 % per second. Going from "
"6 A to 32 A takes about one minute."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adjusting-the-power
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "Less power is implemented immediately."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-adjusting-the-power
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"The power is rounded to the levels that the wallbox can do (e.g. whole "
"amperes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Car is full"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-car-is-full
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"If the car charges at less than 500 W for 5 minutes even though power is "
"released, OpenEMS assumes that it is full. It is then no longer allocated "
"any surplus until it absorbs power again."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-several-charge-points
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "With several charge points, the cluster distributes the surplus:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-several-charge-points
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"First, each car in surplus mode receives its **minimum power**, as long as "
"the surplus is sufficient."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-several-charge-points
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "It distributes the rest according to the set strategy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Strategy\n"
"| Distribution of the rest\n"
"\n"
"| **Even** (default)\n"
"| All cars receive the same additional amount.\n"
"| **By priority**\n"
"| The order of the charge points in the cluster setting decides. The first receives as much as possible, then the next.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"Cars in “PV Surplus with guaranteed charge” or “Fast Charging” mode receive "
"their power regardless of the surplus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase switching"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why switch?"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-why-switch
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "A car needs a minimum power, typically 6 A per phase:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Charging with\n"
"| Minimum power (6 A)\n"
"| Maximum power (16 A)\n"
"\n"
"| 1 phase\n"
"| approx. 1.4 kW\n"
"| approx. 3.7 kW\n"
"| 3 phases\n"
"| approx. 4.1 kW\n"
"| approx. 11 kW\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"Three-phase charging therefore needs at least around 4.1 kW of surplus. "
"**Single-phase charging with solar power is possible from around 1.4 kW.** "
"With plenty of sun, on the other hand, three-phase is faster."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-prerequisites
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"The **wallbox** must support phase switching. In the code, this is provided "
"for Alfen, Hardy Barth, KEBA and Mennekes, among others, depending on the "
"model and equipment. Exception: The Mennekes Professional is controlled via "
"the charging current and does not switch phases automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-prerequisites
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"The **car** must be able to tolerate a charging interruption (setting “Does "
"this EV support interrupting a charging session?” on the vehicle, default: "
"yes). Otherwise, some older vehicles abort the charging process. If this is "
"switched off, switching only takes place while not charging."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-prerequisites
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"Phase switching must be switched on in the charge point control (default: "
"off)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Behavior\n"
"\n"
"| **Off** (default)\n"
"| no switching, the wallbox stays as it is\n"
"| **1-phase**\n"
"| switches to 1 phase as soon as charging starts and 3 phases are currently active\n"
"| **3-phase**\n"
"| switches to 3 phases as soon as charging starts and 1 phase is currently active\n"
"| **Automatic Phase Switching**\n"
"| selects by itself depending on the surplus and charging mode\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual switching"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-manual-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"With “1-phase” or “3-phase” you set the number of phases. OpenEMS switches "
"once as soon as the car charges and then stays there. This is suitable, for "
"example, for vehicles that only charge single-phase or if you always want to "
"charge three-phase at full power."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatic switching"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-automatic-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"In automatic mode, OpenEMS decides based on the power that it **would like "
"to give** the car:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Direction\n"
"| Condition\n"
"\n"
"| 1 → 3 phases\n"
"| Over the last **2 minutes**, the possible power was at least **4,100 W**. Short upward peaks are not counted.\n"
"| 3 → 1 phase\n"
"| Over the last **2 minutes**, the possible power was at most **3,700 W**, and in the last 20 seconds it would have been sufficient for single-phase charging. Short downward dips are not counted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"The gap between 4,100 W and 3,700 W prevents constant switching back and "
"forth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "A **lock time of 5 minutes** applies after each automatic switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Start charging single-phase:** If charging is paused and the wallbox is "
"set to 3 phases, but the surplus is sufficient for single-phase charging "
"(for 10 seconds), OpenEMS switches to 1 phase and starts charging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**In “PV Surplus” mode**, OpenEMS switches between 1 and 3 phases depending "
"on the surplus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**In “PV Surplus with guaranteed charge” mode**, it charges single-phase at "
"the lowest power without surplus, and with surplus as with surplus charging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "**In “Fast Charging” mode**, it charges three-phase at full power."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"If a switch is imminent, OpenEMS provides the expected time (about 100 "
"seconds in advance) as a value of the charge point control."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What happens when switching"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-when-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Stop charging:** The power is set to 0 until the car no longer draws any "
"power."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-when-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Wait:** 30-second pause so that the car and wallbox are safely at rest."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-when-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid "**Switch:** The wallbox changes the number of phases."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-when-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Restart:** Charging starts at minimum power and is then ramped up again."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-when-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"If switching does not succeed within **10 minutes**, OpenEMS aborts and "
"reports a phase switching error."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-when-switching
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"A switch therefore takes at least about half a minute without charging. For "
"this reason, OpenEMS only switches if the situation proves stable over a "
"longer period of time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Together with time schedules and electricity prices"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-together-with-time-schedules-and-electricity-prices
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"In addition to fixed modes, the time schedule of a charge point can also "
"contain “smart” entries with a **minimum charging amount**. For such charge "
"points, the energy optimizer itself plans when to charge in which mode. It "
"primarily uses surplus and, with a xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-"
"tariffs.adoc[time-of-use tariff], cheap times. The result can be seen in the "
"xref:user/schedule/overview.adoc[schedule]. Without such entries, the set "
"mode simply applies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The page xref:user/ev-charging-control/wallbox-comparison.adoc[Wallbox "
"control compared] compares wallbox control with evcc and openWB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/io-control/heat-pumps-and-heating-elements.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-frequently-asked-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Why does the car charge even though there is no surplus?** Either “PV "
"Surplus with guaranteed charge” or “Fast Charging” mode is active, or "
"charging is still in the pause delay (1 minute) or the lock time (5 minutes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-frequently-asked-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Why does charging not start even though the sun is shining?** The surplus "
"must be sufficient for the minimum power, i.e. around 4.1 kW for three-"
"phase. Remedy: automatic phase switching. In addition, the lock time may "
"still be running after a pause."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-frequently-asked-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Why does the home storage not charge?** The car has priority during "
"surplus charging."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-frequently-asked-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
msgid ""
"**Why does the wallbox not switch?** Phase switching is off, the wallbox or "
"car does not support it, the lock time is still running, or the power has "
"not yet been stably above or below the threshold for 2 minutes."
msgstr ""
